    created: "2026-10-29T19:54:24Z",
    prompt: "Transform <image1> into a woven tapestry telling the story of the subject taking selfies, hanging in a great hall from Victorian, visible weave, candlelight. Keep the subject recognisable. Present day: smartphones with glowing screens, e-scooters with chrome frames parked near picnic blankets, sandwiches and fruit arranged on patterned blankets, all rendered in the style of Georges Seurat’s pointillism with visible, luminous dots and rich, textured color gradients. The tapestry hangs in a grand Victorian hall with arched windows, gilded frames, and candlelight flickering on ornate tapestry rods; the weave is visibly textured with threads catching the light, and the composition is framed by heavy velvet drapes and carved wood beams. The figures are rendered with meticulous detail: a woman in a dark top hat and silk dress holds a phone aloft, a man in a waistcoat and bowler hat captures a selfie with a scooter beside him, children in period-appropriate attire play with digital toys, and the picnic blankets are adorned with geometric patterns and bold colors. The setting includes a sun-dappled lawn, distant sailboats on the river, and trees with thick, textured bark—rendered in the style of Seurat’s “A Sunday Afternoon on the Island of La Grande Jatte,” with precise, luminous dots and atmospheric perspective. The lighting is warm, golden, and directional, mimicking candlelight in the hall and filtered sunlight in the scene. Colors are rich, saturated, and carefully layered: deep reds, emerald greens, cobalt blues, and golds. Materials are tactile: silk, velvet, polished wood, and woven canvas. Texture is emphasized: the tapestry’s weave is coarse and visible, the fabrics are thick and detailed, the metal of the e-scooters gleams, and the phone screens emit soft, glowing light. All elements are preserved from the original subject and style, with no added subjects.",
